THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL - playwright-e2e-testing

This directory is somebody else's work, bundled into RichOS. It is not
RichOS-authored and it is not covered by this repository's AGPL.

  Source     https://github.com/bobmatnyc/claude-mpm-skills
  Skill      toolchains/javascript/testing/playwright
  Revision   a0632b527e53d377e186e16b3b8edb8bc2892a98 (2025-12-31)
  Terms      MIT, from the upstream LICENSE file at that revision, reproduced
             verbatim below

VERIFIED 2026-09-04. Every revision of the upstream file was fetched and
compared; this one differs from the bundled SKILL.md by exactly ONE line, and
the frontmatter - including the name playwright-e2e-testing, which upstream
chose - matches it exactly.

THE ONE LINE, so that "modified" means something specific here. In the
form-filling example, upstream writes:

    await page.type('textarea[name="message"]', 'Hello', { delay: 100 });

and the bundled copy writes:

    await page.locator('textarea[name="message"]').fill('Hello');

That is a substitution of a deprecated Playwright API for its replacement.
Nothing in this repository's surviving history records who made it or when -
the history predating 2026-08-20 was rewritten - so no cause is asserted.

Upstream also ships a metadata.json beside the skill, declaring
"license": "MIT". It is not bundled here; it is named because it is a second,
independent statement of the same grant.

